# Who must review what.
#
# This matters more here than in most repos. The eval suite runs with this repo's
# Anthropic credentials, and from the merge queue it runs a contributor's code —
# there is no sandbox for that and there cannot be one. The control is that a
# maintainer read the diff before queueing it, and CODEOWNERS is what makes that
# review happen rather than depend on who noticed the PR.
#
# Only effective once the protected branch requires review from code owners
# (Settings -> Rules / Branch protection).

# Everything, by default.
*                           @Unity-Technologies/plastic-tech-team

# CI and repository automation: a change here changes what runs with our credentials,
# or what is published.
/.github/                   @Unity-Technologies/plastic-tech-team

# The eval suite is executable: promptfooconfig.yaml, run-evals.sh and package.json
# all run in the job that holds the credential.
/evals/                     @Unity-Technologies/plastic-tech-team
